That's the whole point of the Lethe patch.  To make Gehenom
more interesting.  You're supposed to be worried.


> 18 +6 dark elven daggers and a +5 Sword of Balance

The sword of balance is pretty good (silver short sword), but
don't you have a better weapon?  Even going through
gehenom, I would expect Mojo to be a little better (flat +24
to damage).  I assume you're using the daggers as the main
damage-doing weapon?  Killing your enemies fast enough is
the key to not getting hit by a bunch of nasties.

> oodles of blank scrolls and holy/unholy water.

Well, with the Lethe right there....  Just don't go for a swim.
(I always wear an amulet of flying).

> I also have a level 49 pet purple worm named BigGulp!

Trez cool.  I assume he's been hit with a wand of
speed monster?

> tinkered one up from a crystal ball.  I was using it to
> magic-map Hell, but perhaps I should improve my armor
> instead.

Extreme negative armor helps only with damage reduction.
Of course, in Slashem the monsters can hit a *lot* harder.
Also, Hell is not nearly has tedious to map in Lethe.

>
> There are three peaceful temples I have found in the game
> so far - haven't killed the priests.  No Ludios that I have found
> so far.

Have you been to the Black Market?  Sam almost always has a
magic marker or two (be willing to pay a lot for it).

> I plan on using most of the potions of gain level as a extra-fast
